# Conventional Commits

## Format
```
<type>(<scope>): <subject>

[optional body — why, not what]

[optional footer: BREAKING CHANGE, Closes #issue]
```

## Types
| Type | Use |
|------|-----|
| `feat` | New feature |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Code change, no behavior change |
| `test` | Adding or fixing tests |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `chore` | Tooling, deps, config |
| `ci` | CI/CD pipeline |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |

## Scopes
`identity` · `authorization` · `tenants` · `api` · `infra` · `tests` · `docs` · `ci` · `docker` · `ai`

## Rules
- Subject ≤72 chars, imperative mood, no period.
- Body: explain *why*, not *what* (code shows what).
- `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer required for any public contract change.
- Never scope to a file name — use the bounded context or layer.

## Examples
```
feat(identity): add refresh token rotation
fix(authorization): prevent role assignment to non-existent tenant
test(tenants): add integration test for tenant isolation
ci: add Trivy HIGH/CRITICAL gate to build-push workflow
```
